---
import LiveRex from './LiveRex.astro';
---

<main class="workrex-home">
  <p class="eyebrow">Workrex for Rex</p>
  <h1>Parallel agents, separate worktrees.</h1>
  <p class="intro">
    Give each task a Git branch, working directory, and Rex session. Inspect
    progress in one dashboard and merge the work when it is ready.
  </p>
  <nav aria-label="Get started">
    <a href="/workrex/guide/quick-start/">Quick start</a>
    <a href="/workrex/guide/installation/">Install</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/kong109/workrex">Source</a>
  </nav>
  <LiveRex />
  <h2>One terminal model</h2>
  <p>
    A Rex session contains tabs, each represented by a Rex window. Agent
    terminals are blocks. Workrex keeps these IDs scoped to the selected server
    and records the targets it creates.
  </p>
  <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kong109/workrex/main/scripts/install-workrex.sh | bash</code></pre>
  <h2>Follow the whole task</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/workrex/guide/skills/">Agent skills</a> dispatch and coordinate worktrees.
    The <a href="/workrex/guide/dashboard/">dashboard</a> and <a
      href="/workrex/guide/sidebar/">sidebar</a
    > show questions, output, and Git changes. <a href="/workrex/guide/remote/"
      >Remote workspaces</a
    > keep agents running on a server and show their native Rex sessions in the app.
  </p>
</main>

<style>
  .workrex-home {
    max-width: 64rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    color: #339b88;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  h1 {
    max-width: 46rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4.2rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }
  .intro {
    max-width: 43rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }
  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  pre {
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid #718781;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
